This looks like an arugula salad with a few asparagus spears and a small piece of radicchio, on a square white plate of about 26 cm. The greens cover roughly 12 cm by 14 cm and are piled loosely. Arugula is light, so I estimate about 40 g of it. Three asparagus spears add about 50 g. The dressing looks like a light sheen of oil, maybe 1 teaspoon, which is about 40 kcal and 5 g. There may also be a little cheese, which I'll count as 5 g. That puts the total at about 100 g.

Energy: arugula about 10 kcal, asparagus about 10 kcal, dressing about 50 kcal, and cheese and radicchio about 10 kcal, for roughly 80 kcal. I'll round up to 90 kcal to allow for a little extra dressing.

